From f383cfdef0ebb69aadb04c3f039372c6c501d1c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alan Carvalho de Assis <acassis@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 10:19:57 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] cdp1802: add -minline-calls, -minline-compare and
 -minline-shifts

Three options, all off by default (the default output is unchanged):

-minline-calls: a call to a known address pushes the return address
itself (low byte first, as the NCRT call routine does) and branches:
"ldi lo; stxd; ldi hi; stxd; lbr f" is 11 machine cycles instead of
about 37 through the NCRT routine, and 6 bytes more per call.  X is 2
at every call site.  Indirect calls still use __call_reg.

-minline-compare: 16-bit comparisons are expanded inline instead of
calling __cmphi_*; a constant second operand is used as an immediate
(the predicate of cbranchhi4 accepts it only with this option, so the
default register allocation does not change).

-minline-shifts: 16-bit shifts by a constant are expanded inline
instead of calling __ashlhi3, __lshrhi3 or __ashrhi3.

Signed-off-by: Alan Carvalho de Assis <acassis@gmail.com>
Generated-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (claude-opus-5-5) via Claude Code
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
